- 2026-10-06 Windows host run updated WSL to 3.0.1.0 and shut WSL down as that script required; safe sparse conversion then refused. On 2026-10-07 `cp -p` backed up both scripts and `apply_patch` replaced them with ASCII PowerShell 5.1-compatible versions. The Windows PowerShell parser passed both. The final corrected host verifier passed start/config, memory, CPU, swap, VHDX status, sparse-skip, and `wslview`; it reported `systemd degraded` with one failed unit and measured 0 CheckConnection events over its 120-second window. A first test found bare `swapon` is not in WSL `--exec` PATH; the script now uses `/usr/sbin/swapon`. A first port-probe attempt had PowerShell/Bash quoting failure and was removed; separate WSL-side TCP checks passed both Obsidian endpoints. The 75-second idle test is not yet run because this editor is active.
- 2026-10-07 post-update host-health check returned `systemd degraded`, with only `systemd-binfmt.service` failed; its journal details are no longer available. The current interop registration exists and wslview passes, but the failed unit remains unresolved. Kernel scan returned zero storage/I/O/OOM/panic matches. Added the same systemd check to the post-update script; parser and command passed, and the warning output was reproduced.
